        "heading": "ABOUT THE COURSE",
        "heading_style": "section",
        "text": "<p><strong>Certified Professional Groomer (CPG) </strong> </p><p>Class size: &nbsp;Maximum 6 students</p><p>Learners must demonstrate practical skills in</p><ul><li>Safe handling, bathing, drying, and trimming of a toy breed (small frame and/or senior dog)</li><li>Safe handling, bathing, drying, and trimming of a double-coated breed</li></ul><p>Knowledge and understanding will cover: </p><ul><li>Animal welfare and canine wellbeing</li><li>Canine skeletal structure, anatomy, and balance</li><li>Creating style, shape, and symmetry in grooming</li><li>Use and care of grooming tools: blades, scissors, blenders, chunkers</li><li>Grooming techniques for toy breeds and double coats</li><li>Dematting and coat management</li><li>Continued Professional Development (CPD)</li></ul><p><strong>Assessment Structure </strong></p><p>Practical<strong> </strong>Examinations (Two components)</p><p>1. Toy Breed Groom </p><ul><li>Dog must be from the Toy Group</li><li>Must have a trimmable coat</li><li>Under 10” (25cm) at withers and weigh under 10lb (5kg)</li><li>Dog to be pre-bathed and prepared</li><li>Time Allowed: 45 minutes</li><li>Pass Mark: 86% or above </li></ul><p>2. Double-Coated Breed Groom </p><ul><li>Dog must be unbathed at the start of the exam</li><li>Includes full bathing, drying, and grooming</li><li>Time Allowed: 90 minutes(Extra time may be granted for very large breeds)</li><li>Pass Mark: 86% or above</li></ul><p><strong>Written Examination</strong></p><ul><li>50 questions (True/False and Multiple Choice)</li><li>All questions are based on the official Study Guide</li><li>Time Allowed: 30 minutes </li><li>Open Book: Pass mark 92% or above</li><li>Non-Open Book: Pass mark 86% or above</li></ul><p><strong>Study Guide Topics Include:</strong></p><ul><li>Advanced scissoring techniques</li><li>Toy Breed Grooming</li><li>Double Coat Grooming</li><li>Skeletal structure and canine anatomy</li><li>Shape creation, balance, angulation, and diagonal lines</li><li>Dematting techniques</li><li>Further Continuing Professional Development (CPD)</li></ul>",
